{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Target the Spring Cloud Stream (s-c-s) processor model for U1-U5: each ported module becomes a Spring Boot application/processor built on the s-c-s binding abstraction (Processor channels: input/output), following the existing conventions of the s-c-s repository.",
    "Reuse the original Spring XD module business logic and test cases wherever possible; porting effort is focused on adaptation to the s-c-s programming model, Spring Boot auto-configuration, and externalized configuration properties classes, not on re-implementing functionality from scratch.",
    "U1 (json-to-tuple) will depend on/port the Spring XD Tuple library (spring-tuple) for Tuple representation and use Jackson for JSON parsing.",
    "U2 (object-to-json) will use Jackson ObjectMapper for serialization, exposing common mapper options as configuration properties.",
    "U3 (script) will be implemented on top of JSR-223 (javax.script) with Groovy as the default script engine; script location (inline vs. file) and variable bindings are exposed as configuration properties.",
    "U4 (shell) will be implemented using java.lang.ProcessBuilder with streamed stdout/stderr handling, configurable working directory, environment, and execution timeout.",
    "U5 (splitter) will follow Spring Integration splitter semantics using SpEL expressions for split logic, with support for delimiters and correlation/sequence handling.",
    "U6 and U7 are exploration (spike) stories: deliverables are an analysis/findings document plus a throwaway prototype demonstrating the recommended option, not production-hardened code.",
    "U7 spike will use Apache Curator as the ZooKeeper client for persisting composed job definitions and for the recovery/recreate prototype.",
    "U8 (BinderFactory) will be designed as a small SPI/API (factory interface plus binder-type resolution), discovered via Spring Boot auto-configuration/classpath scanning, and validated against at least two binder implementations (e.g., Kafka and Rabbit) to prove the abstraction."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The original Spring XD source code for the json-to-tuple, object-to-json, script, shell, and splitter modules, including their tests, is available for reference and reuse.",
    "The target s-c-s repository already exists with established build conventions (Maven/Gradle parent build, module layout) and a working CI pipeline; only new module additions are required.",
    "The developer is experienced with Spring XD, Spring Integration, Spring Boot, and Spring Cloud Stream, so no significant learning curve is included.",
    "Estimates cover design, implementation, unit and integration testing, documentation, and review/rework cycles; they exclude project management, release operations beyond basic packaging, and long-term maintenance.",
    "All work is performed by a single developer; estimates are effort (work-hours), not elapsed duration, and assume focused, uninterrupted work.",
    "Test infrastructure is available locally or in CI (embedded/in-memory message broker for s-c-s tests, local ZooKeeper instance for the U7 spike, Linux-style shell environment for U4 tests).",
    "U6 and U7 scope ends at a documented recommendation with a working prototype; any subsequent production implementation from those recommendations is out of scope for this increment.",
    "No external code review is required; review effort is covered as self-review and rework cycles within the activities.",
    "Java and Spring versions follow the existing s-c-s repository baseline; no JDK or framework migration work is required."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A01",
      "activity_name": "Repository and build setup for new processor modules",
      "activity_description": "Create module skeletons in the s-c-s repository (parent POM/Gradle wiring, dependency management, CI job configuration) so the five ported processor modules (U1-U5) can be developed and built consistently.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A02",
      "activity_name": "U1: Analyze XD json-to-tuple module and define porting approach",
      "activity_description": "Review the existing XD json-to-tuple module (code, tests, options), identify dependencies (spring-tuple, Jackson), and map XD options to s-c-s configuration properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A03",
      "activity_name": "U1: Implement json-to-tuple processor",
      "activity_description": "Port the json-to-tuple conversion logic to an s-c-s Processor, including configuration properties class and Spring Boot auto-configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A04",
      "activity_name": "U1: Unit and integration tests for json-to-tuple",
      "activity_description": "Port and extend unit tests and add integration tests that run the processor against the s-c-s test binder, covering valid/invalid JSON and nested structures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A05",
      "activity_name": "U1: Documentation for json-to-tuple",
      "activity_description": "Write module README with usage, options, and examples; verify configuration metadata generation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A06",
      "activity_name": "U2: Analyze XD object-to-json module and define porting approach",
      "activity_description": "Review the existing XD object-to-json module (code, tests, options) and map its behavior and options to the s-c-s processor model.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A07",
      "activity_name": "U2: Implement object-to-json processor",
      "activity_description": "Port object-to-JSON serialization (Jackson-based) to an s-c-s Processor with configuration properties and auto-configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A08",
      "activity_name": "U2: Unit and integration tests for object-to-json",
      "activity_description": "Port and extend tests covering payload types, mapper options, and end-to-end processing through the s-c-s test binder.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A09",
      "activity_name": "U2: Documentation for object-to-json",
      "activity_description": "Write module README with usage, options, and examples.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U3: Analyze XD script module and script-engine requirements",
      "activity_description": "Review the XD script module, determine JSR-223 engine support (Groovy default), script location handling, and variable binding requirements for the s-c-s port.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U3: Implement script processor",
      "activity_description": "Port the script-evaluating processor to s-c-s: script source resolution (inline/file), engine management, variable bindings, and configuration properties/auto-configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U3: Unit and integration tests for script processor",
      "activity_description": "Port and extend tests across supported script languages, script-from-file vs inline, error handling, and binder integration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U3: Documentation for script processor",
      "activity_description": "Write module README covering engine setup, options, and example scripts.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U4: Analyze XD shell module and define porting approach",
      "activity_description": "Review the XD shell module (command execution, stdout/stderr handling, options) and design the s-c-s processor adaptation including process lifecycle management.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U4: Implement shell processor",
      "activity_description": "Implement process spawning via ProcessBuilder, streaming of stdout to the output channel, stderr/error handling, configurable environment/working directory/timeout, plus configuration properties and auto-configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "U4: Unit and integration tests for shell processor",
      "activity_description": "Write tests for successful commands, non-zero exit codes, timeouts, streaming output, and binder integration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "U4: Documentation for shell processor",
      "activity_description": "Write module README with usage, options, security considerations, and examples.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "U5: Analyze XD splitter module and define porting approach",
      "activity_description": "Review the XD splitter module (SpEL expression splitting, delimiters, correlation) and map options to s-c-s configuration properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "U5: Implement splitter processor",
      "activity_description": "Port the splitter to an s-c-s Processor using Spring Integration splitter semantics with SpEL expression support, delimiters, and sequence/correlation handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "U5: Unit and integration tests for splitter",
      "activity_description": "Port and extend tests for expression-based splitting, collection/delimited payloads, and binder integration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "U5: Documentation for splitter",
      "activity_description": "Write module README with usage, options, and examples.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "U6: Analyze current composed-job implementation and footprint",
      "activity_description": "Study how composed jobs are created/executed, identify unused resources and memory footprint, and catalog cleanup points and dependencies on composed-job behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "U6: Explore removal alternatives and build spike prototype",
      "activity_description": "Investigate options to remove composed jobs (e.g., replacing with lightweight composition or delegation), and prototype the most promising option to validate feasibility.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "U6: Produce findings report with recommendation",
      "activity_description": "Document analyzed options, prototype results, risks, migration impact, and a concrete recommendation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A25",
      "activity_name": "U7: Analyze composed-job definition storage and recovery requirements",
      "activity_description": "Define what composed-job definition metadata must be persisted, consistency needs, and failure/recovery scenarios the ZooKeeper-based approach must cover.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A26",
      "activity_name": "U7: Spike ZooKeeper-based definition persistence and job recreation",
      "activity_description": "Prototype storing composed-job definitions as ZK metadata (via Curator), reading them back, and recreating jobs from the repository after a simulated failure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A27",
      "activity_name": "U7: Document options, trade-offs, and recommendation",
      "activity_description": "Write the findings document covering ZK data layout, consistency/failure behavior, alternatives considered, and recommendation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A28",
      "activity_name": "U8: Design BinderFactory API/SPI",
      "activity_description": "Design the BinderFactory abstraction: factory interface, binder-type resolution strategy, configuration model, and discovery mechanism (auto-configuration/classpath based).",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A29",
      "activity_name": "U8: Implement core BinderFactory abstraction",
      "activity_description": "Implement the factory, binder registration/lookup, lifecycle handling, and default binder-type resolution.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A30",
      "activity_name": "U8: Integrate existing binding infrastructure with BinderFactory",
      "activity_description": "Refactor the current binder creation/wiring code to go through the new abstraction without breaking existing single-binder behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A31",
      "activity_name": "U8: Unit and integration tests for BinderFactory",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for resolution/registration logic and integration tests exercising the abstraction with two different binder types to prove multi-binder support.",
      "most_likely_effort": 18
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A32",
      "activity_name": "U8: Documentation for BinderFactory",
      "activity_description": "Document the new abstraction, how to add a new binder type, and migration notes for existing users.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A33",
      "activity_name": "Cross-increment review and rework",
      "activity_description": "Self-review cycles, static analysis cleanup, consistency checks across all modules, and rework arising from reviews of U1-U8 deliverables.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A34",
      "activity_name": "Final integration, packaging, and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "End-to-end build verification, dependency/version alignment across modules, packaging of the processor artifacts, and release notes preparation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 338
  }
}

